WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.220
SCP-682 Vs SCP-3108.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:08.901
The Hard to Destroy Reptile may treat all
regular firearms like mere annoyances, but

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:12.370
could the legendary Nerfing Gun take the monster
down a peg or two?

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:17.000
The Nerfing Gun has the power to turn anything
it shoots into a worse version of itself.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.820
A D-Class was ordered to shoot 682 with it,
and after missing six times due to fear, he

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.199
landed the lucky seventh shot.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:25.890
But it wasn’t so lucky.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:31.240
682 became larger, stronger, and developed
the ability to explode and reconstitute itself

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.440
immediately as an offensive weapon.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.460
It breached containment and killed many members
of personnel.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:41.020
Researcher Westrin theorized that 682 became
a more dangerous version of itself because

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:47.280
a weaker, more docile version of 682 would
be considered a net positive by the SCP Foundation,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.000
and therefore wouldn’t technically be making
it worse.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.229
That’s one dangerous technicality.

